    "Tallyist" : {
      "comment" : "The wordmark displayed in the footer of the share card.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Tallyist does not collect your data. Nothing you log leaves your control." : {
      "shouldTranslate" : false
    },
    "Tallyist is free, private, and has nothing to sell you. If it earns a place on your home screen, you can buy its maker a drink. Tips unlock nothing — everyone gets the whole app." : {

    },
    "Tallyist keeps a record of what you drink so you can see your own pattern. It doesn't set goals, keep streaks, or offer advice." : {
      "comment" : "A paragraph describing the primary function of the app.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Tap the widget's log button, then come back here. \"never ran\" means the tap didn't reach the intent at all; anything starting \"failed\" means the write itself broke. Store mode is what was asked for when the store opened; iCloud sync is what actually happened, and they can disagree — a store opens fine with CloudKit requested and no iCloud account, then simply never syncs. \"IN MEMORY\" means nothing is being saved at all." : {

    },
    "Terms of Use" : {
      "comment" : "A link to the app's terms of use.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "That didn't go through. Nothing was charged." : {

    },
    "That's lower than roughly %lld%% of US adults who drink." : {

    },
    "That's more than roughly %lld%% of US adults who drink." : {

    },
    "The app couldn't open its storage, so drinks logged in this session won't be kept. Restarting the app usually resolves this." : {

    },
    "The drinks you log — type, size, strength, and when. Days recorded as alcohol-free — by you, or by another app that recorded zero drinks in Apple Health. Your settings, such as which region's standard-drink definition your totals use.\n\nAll of it is stored on your device, in the app's own database. There are no accounts and no sign-up." : {
      "shouldTranslate" : false
    },
    "The optional tip jar is processed entirely by Apple through your App Store account, exactly like any App Store purchase: Tallyist never sees your payment details, and Apple tells the app only that a purchase completed. Tips unlock nothing, and nothing about tipping — or not — appears in or affects your drink log. Recurring tips can be cancelled any time in your App Store subscription settings, and the app offers a local reminder a week before each renewal so you can cancel before being charged." : {
      "shouldTranslate" : false
    },
    "The widget follows the device's appearance either way." : {

    },
    "This is the unit your totals are shown in. Changing it re-expresses everything, including past days — what you drank doesn't change, only how it's counted." : {

    },
    "This policy is published in a public repository at github.com/semmes/Tallyist; every change to it, and its date, is visible in that repository's history. If a future version of the app ever collects data, this policy and the App Store privacy labels will change before that version ships." : {
      "shouldTranslate" : false
    },
